<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27438" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίς</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>twice, doubly,</i> with Nouns,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τόσσον</span>
			<i>twice</i> as much, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.491
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.57
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀληθὴς ὁ λόγος ὡς δ. παῖς γέρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. παῖδες οἱ γέροντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theopomp.Com.
					69
				</span></i>
			: more freq. with Verbs, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦτο δ. ἤδη ἐγένετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.104
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. φράσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					173
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1384
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. αἰάζειν καὶ τρίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					432
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. καὶ τρίς φασι καλὸν εἶναι τὰ καλὰ
					λέγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					498e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				60a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. βιῶναι</span>”
				<i>twice over,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					223.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δειπνεῖν . . δ. τῆς ἡμέρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					207
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>Mith.</u>
					78
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δ. Νέωνος,</span>
			=
			<i>son and grandson</i> of N., <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				3092.18
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Aegosthena</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αὐρήλιος Αὐξάνων δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BCH</u>
					17.249
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Apamea</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αὐρ. Δοῦ&lt;ρ&gt;λος δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>JHS</u>
					19.301
				</span></i>
			 (Selmea [Lycaonia]).—In compds. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι-,</span> but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δισ-</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δισμύριοι, δισχίλιοι,
				δισθανής, δίσαβος, δισάρπαγος, δίσευνος,</span> etc. (Cf.
			Skt. <i>dvis</i> 'twice', Lat. <i>bis.</i>)</div>
